/-!
# Explicit Hall–Janko centric census nodes

The 142 nodes are given by four generators (with identity padding), together
with binary membership tables. Positive words prove membership in the generated
subgroups; right multiplication by generators and inverse generators proves
the reverse inclusion. Thus all membership tables are checked in Lean.
Completeness of the family is a separate maximal-descent certificate.

Source: the presentation in `SylowPresentations`; Janko–Thompson, Math. Z.
113 (1970), Theorem 1.4, p.386 and application p.395; MacWilliams,
Trans. AMS 150 (1970), DOI 10.1090/S0002-9947-1970-0276324-3.
-/

